course: dictionary
lesson: 9880
title: Tactical: plans, moves and clever words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tactical is about the plans and moves you use to win a game, a battle or a contest. «The coach made a tactical substitution in the second half.» The word tells you the change was planned to help the team win, not just a random swap.
explain: Tactical can also mean done carefully now to get an advantage later. «Sam made a tactical choice to save his energy for the final lap.» The clues are save his energy and final lap: he chose now, so he would be stronger when it mattered.
explain: Some adults use tactical to make a hard thing sound smoother. «"Tactical redeployment" is military jargon for a retreat.» Jargon is special, technical words used by one group. A retreat means pulling back, so when you meet a fancy phrase, swap in a plainer meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Tactical means to do with the plans and moves used to win a game, battle or contest.
fact: A tactical decision is one done carefully to get an advantage later.
fact: Tactical appears in sport, chess, history and everyday choices.
fact: «Tactical redeployment» is military jargon for a retreat.
fact: Armies and governments sometimes use technical-sounding words to hide how harsh an action really is, so always check what a fancy word means.
exercise: «The coach made a tactical substitution in the second half.» What does tactical mean here? | *Planned to help the team win | Done in a hurry with no plan | A substitution about food | A swap made by accident
exercise: «Sam made a tactical choice to save his energy for the final lap.» What does tactical mean here? | Done in the dark | Done to make everyone laugh | Done by accident | *Done carefully to get an advantage later
exercise: «"Tactical redeployment" is military jargon for a retreat.» What does retreat mean? | *Pulling back | Cheering loudly | Charging forward | Eating lunch
test: Why might someone use the long phrase «tactical redeployment» instead of the word retreat? | *To make a pull-back sound less harsh | To prove they had won the battle | To make the sentence more fun to read | To make the report shorter
test: Which sentence uses tactical to mean a planned move in a game? | *The chess player made a tactical move to trap the queen | I ate a tactical sandwich for lunch | I felt tactical and sleepy | The tactical rain fell all afternoon
exam: Which best describes a tactical decision? | A decision made only because a rule book says so | Done without any thought at all | *Done carefully now to gain an advantage later | A decision about the weather
